# BW-80 (Machine 140): the ZX80 issue 2 board's component area, after Grant Searle's foil
# layout (docs/machines/140-bw80/BW80_DESIGN.md). The keyboard area (the ZX80's front 62 mm) is
# left off: the keyboard is a window. Every chip stands with its notch at the back, where Sinclair
# put it; positions are courtyard centres in mm from the back-left corner.
size 155.5 142
at IC1  64.0  66.2         # Z80, the middle
at IC2  134.9 57.2         # ROM, right
at IC3  14.4  48.3         # RAM, back left
at IC4  28.5  48.3
at IC5  90.6  80.1         # data latch
at IC6  109.6 52.1         # ROM address multiplexers
at IC7  109.7 80.1
at IC8  90.5  52.1
at IC9  28.5  76.3         # dots
at IC10 14.4  76.3         # keyboard buffer
at IC11 89.3  111.4        # the gates, the front row: IC14 IC15 IC16 IC13 IC17 IC11 IC12 IC18 IC20
at IC12 105.8 111.4
at IC13 58.9  111.4
at IC14 17.0  111.4
at IC15 29.6  111.4
at IC16 46.2  111.4
at IC17 72.9  111.4
at IC18 118.5 111.4
at IC19 142.5 84.0         # HSYNC
at IC20 131.3 111.4
at IC21 128.5 84.0         # line counter

# The connectors: the expansion bus along the back edge at the left (the ZX80's slot), video where
# the modulator sits, power at the 9 V socket's corner, the keyboard where its tracks left the
# component area.
edge J4 back left
edge J2 back 62%
edge J1 back 88%
edge J3 front 30%

# The passives beside the chips they serve, as the drawing: one resistor column fits between
# the RAM column and IC1, two rows of resistors in the front band.
next R4 IC4 right          # the data bus resistors: a column from beside IC4 down past IC9
next R5 R4 front
next R6 R5 front
next R7 R6 front
next R8 R7 front
next R9 IC9 right
next R10 R9 front
next R11 R10 front
next R12 R11 front
next R1 IC10 front         # EAR, the shift clock, NOP_EN
next R2 R1 front
next R3 R2 front
next R13 IC14 front        # the keyboard pull-ups, a row along the front
next R14 R13 right
next R15 R14 right
next R16 R15 right
next R17 R16 right
next R18 R13 front         # M1 clock, RAM select, the CPU clock pull-up: the second row
next R19 R18 right
next R20 R19 right
next R21 IC1 front         # reset, bus request, wait
next R22 R21 right
next R23 R22 right
next R24 IC11 front        # the load gate, the load pulse
next R25 R24 right
next C11 R25 right
next X1 IC20 right         # the clock
next R28 IC2 right         # MD6 pull-up
next C9 IC15 back          # the shift clock pulse
# RST1 has no rule: it goes free, near RESET_N's parts.
